From a69077032300ff044b959a3c81edf8c8534568c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:12:25 +0200
Subject: [RFC PATCH 1/1] scsi: spi: retry a transient failure of the
 initial DV inquiry

After an IOC reset a Fusion SPI controller can return DID_SOFT_ERROR
for the first inquiry, with no data transferred. Domain validation uses
REQ_FAILFAST_DRIVER, so this retryable result aborts validation and leaves
the target using asynchronous transfers.

Allow bounded retries while obtaining the reference inquiry at narrow
asynchronous settings. Keep the subsequent comparison and transfer-mode
tests fail-fast so retries cannot hide failures at a negotiated speed.

Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/scsi/scsi_transport_spi.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/scsi/scsi_transport_spi.c b/drivers/scsi/scsi_transport_spi.c
index 3e3da8c2ff26..5257a775e138 100644
--- a/drivers/scsi/scsi_transport_spi.c
+++ b/drivers/scsi/scsi_transport_spi.c
@@ -720,10 +720,15 @@ spi_dv_device_compare_inquiry(struct scsi_device *sdev, u8 *buffer,
 	};
 
 	for (r = 0; r < retries; r++) {
-		memset(ptr, 0, len);
+		int retry_count = ptr == buffer ? DV_RETRIES : 0;
 
-		result = spi_execute(sdev, spi_inquiry, REQ_OP_DRV_IN,
-				     ptr, len, NULL);
+		/* Retry only the reference read at narrow asynchronous settings. */
+		do {
+			memset(ptr, 0, len);
+			result = spi_execute(sdev, spi_inquiry, REQ_OP_DRV_IN,
+					     ptr, len, NULL);
+		} while (result == (DID_SOFT_ERROR << 16) && retry_count-- &&
+			 scsi_device_online(sdev));
 		
 		if(result || !scsi_device_online(sdev)) {
 			scsi_device_set_state(sdev, SDEV_QUIESCE);
